3. Wi-Fi Performance Classification
The program will analyze the measurements and classify locations into categories such as:
Good
Moderate
Weak
The classification will be based on predefined thresholds established for the project.
4. Location Comparison
Users can compare Wi-Fi performance between different dormitory locations.
5. Time-Based Analysis
The program can compare measurements taken at different times to identify changes in Wi-Fi performance throughout the day.
6. Wi-Fi Accessibility Map
The program will present the collected data on a dormitory floor plan or simplified map so that users can visually identify areas with stronger or weaker connectivity.
7. Summary Report
The system will generate a summary containing information such as:
Average signal strength
Average download speed
Average upload speed
Average latency
Strongest-performing areas
Areas requiring further investigation

V. Planned Inputs and Outputs
Inputs
The user will provide:
Location — where the measurement was taken
Time and date — when the measurement was taken
Signal strength — measured in dBm
Download speed — measured in Mbps
Upload speed — measured in Mbps
Latency — measured in milliseconds
Example:
Location: Room 12
Time: 7:00 PM
Signal Strength: -68 dBm
Download Speed: 25 Mbps
Upload Speed: 10 Mbps
Latency: 42 ms

Outputs
After processing the information, the program will provide:
1. Performance Classification
Room 12: MODERATE
2. Statistical Summary
Average Download Speed: 25 Mbps
Average Upload Speed: 10 Mbps
Average Latency: 42 ms
3. Location Comparison
The program can display which tested locations have relatively stronger or weaker measurements.
4. Wi-Fi Accessibility Map
The program will display the collected measurements on a simplified dormitory map.
5. Overall Summary
The system can produce a summary of the dormitory's measured Wi-Fi conditions and identify areas that may need further investigation.

